<Base
  title="About"
  description="Super Dad’s Cookbook is Matt’s collection of homemade family recipes. He’s a married dad of five who cooks from scratch to save money and know what’s in his kids’ food."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About this cookbook</h1>
      <p>Homemade food for a big family, written down so you can make it too.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I’m Matt, a married dad of five who loves to cook and loves to feed my family homemade food. Cooking from scratch
        means avoiding a lot of the garbage ingredients that come with food from a bag or a box.
      </p>
      <p>
        Saving money is important to me too, and that’s a big reason I think people should cook at home. So is knowing
        what’s in my kids’ food. Making food kids like can be hard, but it is possible.
      </p>
      <p>
        People are always asking for my recipes, so putting them all in one place just made sense. One day I hope my
        kids will use this site to make the things they grew up eating.
      </p>
      <p>
        By trade, I’m an entrepreneur and web developer with <a href="https://kamastudio.com">KamaStudio</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How the recipes are written</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Everyday measurements: cups, tablespoons and teaspoons. A few baking recipes are weighed in grams, with cup amounts listed too.</li>
        <li>Steps in the order you do them, with a time or a visual cue for when each one is done.</li>
        <li>Ingredients you can find at a regular grocery store.</li>
        <li>Tips at the end for swaps, make-ahead plans and leftovers.</li>
        <li>Some recipes started from other websites. Those are written in my own words with my changes, and link back to the original.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cooking from your phone</h2>
      <p>
        On any recipe, tap an ingredient to cross it off. Use “Keep screen on while cooking” so your phone doesn’t go
        dark halfway through a step, or print the recipe for the fridge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
